;;; Which core a program reported moved with interner ids — M1e2 **W11**,
;;; register row `W11/unsat-core-id-space` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`).
;;; Promoted from `corpus/fuzz_findings/unsat-core-id-space.ein` by S1e2.2.12
;;; (2026-11-04), which stays there as a frontend-fuzzer seed.
;;;
;;; ── What this program was ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The rewritten engine fuzzer's find of 2026-08-21 (`utils/fuzz_engine.py`,
;;; 19 forms minimised to 4): the walk called it `Contradiction` and reported
;;; the core (r1 o4 o5) as interned and (r1 o1 o5) (r1 o4 o1) under a
;;; permuted interner, one build and two answers
;;; (`corpus/fuzz_findings/unsat-core-id-space.md`).
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Root holds (r1 o4 o5) and is consistent. `fire-2` derives (false) from a
;;; two-step r1 chain, or from an r1 fact beside a stored (not (r1 …)), which
;;; no rule writes. Of the five candidates, (r1 o1 o4), (r1 o5 o1) and
;;; (r1 o5 o4) chain with (r1 o4 o5) and are dead alone; (r1 o1 o5) and
;;; (r1 o4 o1) are alive alone and chain with each other. So R is three
;;; states, ∅, {(r1 o1 o5)} and {(r1 o4 o1)}, and N has four members, each
;;; with one derivation of (false) and so one core.
;;;
;;; ── Since M1e2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The walk's `Contradiction` rested on what its search wrote into root, the
;;; kill cache's and the writeback's negatives, which no route writes
;;; (S1e2.1a.5's switch, 2026-10-18; `solve_interface.md` § 0). S1e2.2.12
;;; compared every core a run reports under eight permutations of the
;;; interner, and none of this program's moved; `id_order_invariance`
;;; permutes it per commit.

(relation r1 T T)
(is-a o1 T)
(r1 o4 o5)
(rule fire-2 ()
  :match  (or (and (r1 ?v0 ?v1) (r1 ?v4 ?v0)) (and (r1 ?v0 ?v1) (r1 ?v0 ?v1) (not (r1 ?v2 ?v3))))
  :assert (false))
